# Version 4: Semantic HGT Target Formulation Study

This package keeps the `semantic_v2` graph, K=80 history, split, and two-layer
Semantic HGT fixed while comparing target representations and losses for the next
Event Type, Time Gap, and Position.

## Screened Methods

| Task | Methods |
|---|---|
| Event | `ce`, `inverse_ce`, `sqrt_capped_ce`, `balanced_softmax` |
| Time | `current_huber`, `log1p_huber`, `bucket_offset` |
| Position | `xy`, `zone`, `zone_residual` |

The screen uses the frozen feasibility sample plan (34,048 train and 7,296
validation transitions), seed `20260715`, LR `9e-4`, K=80, batch 256, at most
8 epochs, and patience 2. It never constructs a test loader.

## Commands

```bash
/home/li/anaconda3/bin/python scripts/analyze_targets.py
/home/li/anaconda3/bin/python scripts/run_matrix.py --stage smoke
scripts/launch_screen_background.sh
/home/li/anaconda3/bin/python scripts/run_matrix.py --stage summarize --summary-stage screen
```

The lightweight three-seed confirmation and paired final comparison can be run as
one gated background pipeline:

```bash
scripts/launch_light_pipeline_background.sh
```

Confirmation reuses the completed `20260715` screen and trains only seeds
`20260716–20260717` on the same 34,048/7,296 sample plan. It compares Event
`inverse_ce/ce/sqrt_capped_ce`, Time `current_huber/log1p_huber`, and Position
`xy/zone_residual`. No confirmation job can read test data.

After `winners.json` is locked, the final stage trains paired `joint_original`
and `joint_optimized` models for all three seeds and evaluates their checkpoints
on the complete test split. It also evaluates the selected single-task models to
measure multitask interference. The final report includes a 10,000-iteration
match- and seed-paired bootstrap.

## Joint Loss Scale Validation

The loss-balance pipeline compares Event CE weights `0.05`, `0.10`, and `0.20`
while keeping Time and Position weights at `1.0`. Its fixed objective is
`(w_event * event_loss + time_loss + position_loss) / 3`. Each run records raw
losses, shared-backbone gradient norms, effectively weighted norms, and pairwise
gradient cosines at initialization and at the selected checkpoint.

```bash
scripts/launch_loss_balance_background.sh
```

The nine training jobs use validation only. Full test evaluation is created only
if a three-seed mean passes all four predeclared validation gates relative to J0.
Results are isolated under `experiments/loss_balance_validation`,
`experiments/loss_balance_test`, and `experiments/loss_balance`.

## Frozen Target-Dependency Study

The isolated dependency study caches frozen J2 contexts, attributes paired J2
and NMSTPP position errors, and trains parameter-matched residual probes for
Event-to-Position, Event-to-Time, and Time-to-Position dependencies. Oracle,
predicted, null, and shuffled conditions use identical head capacity.

```bash
scripts/launch_dependency_study_background.sh
```

Train and validation caches are built first. All 42 probe checkpoints must be
locked before the pipeline constructs a full-test cache. Outputs are written to
`experiments/target_dependency_v1`; existing J2 and baseline files are read-only.

The attribution report always exposes two position metrics: continuous
prediction versus true coordinates, and equal-granularity Zone-center distance.
These must not be mixed when comparing HGT with NMSTPP.

## Semantic V3 Possession Regression

The Possession pipeline keeps K=80, the two-layer HGT, `CE x 0.2`,
`current_huber`, and XY decoding fixed. It incrementally evaluates membership,
owner, transition, categorical state, and causal dynamic snapshots from the
independent `semantic_v3_possession` graph.

```bash
scripts/launch_possession_regression_background.sh
```

`N0` first proves that reading the V3 files with all Possession inputs disabled
exactly reproduces Semantic V2. Topology and feature selection use validation
only; complete test predictions and the paired bootstrap are created after the
V3 configuration is locked. Outputs are isolated under
`experiments/possession_regression`.

Outputs are isolated under `experiments/`; target-only descriptive analysis is
written to `artifacts/target_analysis/`. Existing graphs, checkpoints, baseline
repositories, and prior experiment results are read-only dependencies.

## Semantic V3 Subgraph Scale Study

The scale study keeps the selected V3-D2 model and task formulation fixed while
changing only the causally visible Event set. Round A compares F80 with S20,
S40, P1, P2, TR10, and SP30. Round B is launched only when a family reaches its
registered practical effect size, agrees in at least two seeds, and has a paired
95% confidence interval that excludes zero.

```bash
/home/li/anaconda3/bin/python scripts/run_subgraph_matrix.py --stage verify
/home/li/anaconda3/bin/python scripts/run_subgraph_matrix.py --stage stats
scripts/launch_subgraph_scale_background.sh
```

Possession, Transition, and Spatial views do not cross periods. Sparse views
retain original `source_index` gaps and never create synthetic temporal edges.
Transition reports distinguish confirmed switch/restart context, boundary
context, and fallback samples. Spatial jobs are gated by geometry tests for the
anchor-team coordinate transform and 15/30/45 metre boundaries.

All scale selection uses validation only. The full test split is opened only
after task-specific winners and their deterministic size-matched random controls
are locked. Outputs are isolated under `experiments/subgraph_scale_v1`.

## Task-Specific P1/P2 Fusion

The static fusion study compares shared-HGT hard routing (`Fixed-A/B`) with
task-level P1/P2 Softmax weights (`SF-A/B`). Fusion is applied only after the
64-dimensional context projection; it is global per task and never depends on
the sample.

```bash
/home/li/anaconda3/bin/python scripts/run_task_view_fusion_matrix.py --stage verify
scripts/launch_task_view_fusion_background.sh
```

All modes share one encoder, HGT, context projection, and set of nonlinear
heads. Soft fusion adds only four or six scalar logits, initialized from the
validated hard view preferences and excluded from weight decay. Validation
locks all four registered configurations before complete test evaluation.
Reports under `experiments/task_view_fusion_v1` include task-level practical
effects, learned weights, context norms, paired bootstrap intervals, and the
two preregistered entry conditions for later sample-conditioned routing.
# Team/Player Context-Scale Study

`actor_scale_v1` extends the Semantic V3-D2 scale analysis to the two acting
entity targets without introducing soft fusion or a sample-level router.

```text
Team:   F80 / P1 / P2 -> next acting team relative to the anchor team
Player: F80 / P1 / P2 -> next acting player over the match-local roster
```

Team and Player are trained as independent single-task probes. All views use
the same targets, sample order, HGT initialization, and complete pre-match
`lineup + bench` Player candidate set. Only historical Event context changes.
The England source audit found zero event actors outside those pre-match
rosters across all 380 matches. Team reports Accuracy and Macro-F1; Player
reports Top-1/3/5, MRR, target coverage, and candidate count. Validation selects
Team by Macro-F1 and Player by Top-1. Test data is read only after the complete
validation matrix is locked.

Entry points:

```text
scripts/run_actor_scale_experiment.py
scripts/run_actor_scale_matrix.py --stage <verify|smoke|validation|test|summarize|pipeline>
scripts/launch_actor_scale_background.sh
```
# Five-task context-view validation

The `five_task_view_v1` experiment keeps one shared Semantic V3-D2 HGT and
compares three fixed context contracts for next Event, Time, Position, Team,
and Player prediction:

```text
Five-F80:  all tasks use F80
Five-Hard: Event/Time use P2, Position uses P1, Team/Player use F80
Five-Soft: Event/Time/Position learn static P1/P2 weights, Team/Player use F80
```

The fixed joint objective is:

```text
(0.2 Event + Time + Position + 0.05 Team + 0.4 Player) / 3
```

Run the detached pipeline with:

```bash
scripts/launch_five_task_view_background.sh
```

Outputs are isolated under `experiments/five_task_view_v1/`.

# Fixed-budget multitask conflict study

The follow-up `five_task_fixed_budget_v1` study separates training budget from
checkpoint selection. Three-task and five-task matched pairs run all 16 epochs,
matched boundary-hit pairs resume exactly to epoch 24, and conflict localization
uses F80-only T3/T4-Team/T4-Player/T5 models selected by the shared E/T/P loss.
Player private residual capacity is tested only when validation evidence identifies
Player as a conflict source.

```bash
scripts/launch_fixed_budget_conflict_background.sh
```

The pipeline does not read the test split until validation decisions are written
to `experiments/five_task_fixed_budget_v1/decisions/baseline_lock.json`.
